1
00:00:25,420 --> 00:00:28,740
Big roads, small roads, this Yazukuri

2
00:00:28,740 --> 00:00:32,415
Big roads, small roads,

3
00:00:32,465 --> 00:00:34,700
this Yazukuri

4
00:00:34,700 --> 00:00:40,920
Summer has come again this year

5
00:00:42,380 --> 00:00:46,900
Summer has come again this year

6
00:00:48,760 --> 00:00:52,280
Big roads, small roads, this Yazukuri

7
00:00:52,280 --> 00:00:55,200
In the south wind, nibbling

8
00:00:55,200 --> 00:00:58,340
Big bottom, small bottom,
a little bottom, about that size

9
00:00:58,340 --> 00:00:59,760
in red

10
00:00:59,760 --> 00:01:02,960
pri-pri-pri-pri-pri-pri-pri-pri-pri-pri-pri-pri-pri-pri-pri-pri

11
00:01:02,960 --> 00:01:08,480
In the south wind, nibbling

12
00:01:12,060 --> 00:01:14,420
In the south wind, nibbling

13
00:01:17,660 --> 00:01:19,160
wobbling on the shore

14
00:01:19,160 --> 00:01:20,600
wobbling on the shore

15
00:01:28,560 --> 00:01:31,240
The rookie cop who came from the sky

16
00:01:35,080 --> 00:01:37,060
What a beautiful day.

17
00:01:37,060 --> 00:01:40,240
On a day like this,
something good is bound to happen.

18
00:01:42,320 --> 00:01:43,340
It's quiet.

19
00:01:43,340 --> 00:01:44,820
It's too quiet.

20
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:47,280
Which means...

21
00:01:48,660 --> 00:01:50,720
Ryotsu's late again

22
00:01:58,620 --> 00:02:01,620
Hey, Ryotsu's actually doing his work...

23
00:02:01,620 --> 00:02:05,900
He showed up two hours before his
shift and he's been like this ever since.

24
00:02:05,900 --> 00:02:09,200
We were just saying it's
going to rain or something.

25
00:02:09,700 --> 00:02:14,320
I-I'm incredibly moved right now.

26
00:02:14,320 --> 00:02:19,960
In my 30 years as a police officer,
nothing has made me this happy.

27
00:02:19,960 --> 00:02:21,341
Chief,

28
00:02:21,391 --> 00:02:24,540
there's no need to be this moved.

29
00:02:24,540 --> 00:02:28,220
Wow, Ryotsu has finally
woken up to his work.

30
00:02:28,270 --> 00:02:30,360
All my hardships have finally paid off.

31
00:02:31,040 --> 00:02:32,900
Alright, it's done!

32
00:02:33,860 --> 00:02:37,420
Well done, Ryotsu.
I always knew you'd come through someday.

33
00:02:37,760 --> 00:02:40,140
By the way, what paperwork were you writing?

34
00:02:40,520 --> 00:02:43,400
What do you mean? Come on.
Have you forgotten, Chief?

35
00:02:43,760 --> 00:02:45,260
You told me yesterday.

36
00:02:45,720 --> 00:02:47,940
To submit the reprimand
reports that have piled up.

37
00:02:48,960 --> 00:02:50,480
Re-reprimand reports?

38
00:02:51,180 --> 00:02:52,760
I've written them all up.

39
00:02:54,740 --> 00:02:56,380
Your hand has stopped moving.

40
00:02:56,380 --> 00:02:58,240
You idiot!

41
00:03:04,060 --> 00:03:06,120
You, you're something else!

42
00:03:07,320 --> 00:03:09,760
Chief, are you all right?

43
00:03:10,760 --> 00:03:13,240
Sorry, but could you get
me some stomach medicine?

44
00:03:13,240 --> 00:03:13,720
Yes.

45
00:03:15,140 --> 00:03:16,800
Have you been drinking too much, Chief?

46
00:03:16,800 --> 00:03:19,000
You're not getting any younger, you know.

47
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:21,300
You'd better take it easy,
or you'll be in trouble.

48
00:03:21,300 --> 00:03:22,160
What did you say?

49
00:03:22,160 --> 00:03:24,280
Hey! This is all your fault, you hear me!

50
00:03:24,720 --> 00:03:27,193
Chief, calm down! If you get this angry,

51
00:03:27,243 --> 00:03:28,820
you'll burst a blood vessel!

52
00:03:29,120 --> 00:03:30,260
Phew!

53
00:03:32,760 --> 00:03:37,400
Must I just accept that I'm stuck
with such a useless subordinate?

54
00:03:38,580 --> 00:03:42,340
Speaking of subordinates,
Nakagawa hasn't come in yet, has he?

55
00:03:42,780 --> 00:03:43,700
Nakagawa-san?

56
00:03:44,300 --> 00:03:47,400
He's the new recruit being assigned
to this police box starting today.

57
00:03:47,560 --> 00:03:48,820
What kind of person is he?

58
00:03:49,520 --> 00:03:51,680
He's quite handsome, isn't he.

59
00:03:52,360 --> 00:03:54,720
He grew up in New York until he was sixteen?

60
00:03:55,160 --> 00:03:57,940
He's one of those returnee students,
like Reiko.

61
00:03:57,940 --> 00:03:58,400
Yes.

62
00:03:59,340 --> 00:04:01,280
He has a permanent license for cars.

63
00:04:01,280 --> 00:04:03,760
He also has licenses for boats and planes.

64
00:04:04,240 --> 00:04:07,140
On top of that, he's great at
sports and fluent in languages.

65
00:04:07,140 --> 00:04:11,380
His marksmanship is such that he could blow
the head off a pin from a kilometer away.

66
00:04:11,380 --> 00:04:14,120
Who exactly is this Nakagawa, anyway?

67
00:04:14,120 --> 00:04:16,840
He's the heir to the Nakagawa zaibatsu.

68
00:04:19,160 --> 00:04:22,860
Do you mean the Nagakawa Zaibatsu,
one of the top five in the world?

69
00:04:23,600 --> 00:04:27,420
That's right. What's this Nagakawa-whatsit?
Some kind of financial tool shop?

70
00:04:28,800 --> 00:04:32,220
Not financial tool, zaibatsu.
It means conglomerate.

71
00:04:32,600 --> 00:04:33,760
A konjac shop?

72
00:04:33,960 --> 00:04:34,500
Wrong.

73
00:04:35,040 --> 00:04:36,460
No, not that.

74
00:04:36,660 --> 00:04:39,154
Reiko-kun, don't talk to that idiot.

75
00:04:39,204 --> 00:04:41,300
You'll get a headache like I do.

76
00:04:42,320 --> 00:04:43,040
Yes, sir.

77
00:04:43,926 --> 00:04:48,320
A rich brat like that can't handle
the hard work of being a police officer.

78
00:04:48,820 --> 00:04:51,260
He'll whine right away and quit,
that's the punchline.

79
00:04:51,260 --> 00:04:52,500
Then, Ryotsu!

80
00:04:52,700 --> 00:04:56,620
So make sure that doesn't happen,
you train Nakagawa!

81
00:05:04,140 --> 00:05:05,300
Alright, now!

82
00:05:12,900 --> 00:05:15,020
Well? Pretty awesome

83
00:05:15,660 --> 00:05:19,400
It's the combat rescue type of the
U.S. military's Black Hawk helicopter.

84
00:05:19,400 --> 00:05:20,020
Unbelievable.

85
00:05:20,640 --> 00:05:23,820
So that's what you were making
instead of working yesterday.

86
00:05:24,340 --> 00:05:25,060
Well, well.

87
00:05:25,060 --> 00:05:28,460
If Ohara-san finds out,
he's definitely going to blow his top.

88
00:05:32,500 --> 00:05:35,700
That's strange.

89
00:05:35,700 --> 00:05:37,140
What's the remote for, anyway?

90
00:05:37,840 --> 00:05:39,840
What is that locker, anyway?

91
00:05:40,580 --> 00:05:41,720
That's right. I remember now.

92
00:05:45,180 --> 00:05:47,720
When did he buy all
that without us noticing?

93
00:05:47,720 --> 00:05:49,900
You didn't know?

94
00:05:51,220 --> 00:05:53,780
He's completely turned the police
box into his personal property.

95
00:05:58,780 --> 00:06:00,260
Yeah, go on, go on!

96
00:06:03,500 --> 00:06:05,140
Yo, it flew!

97
00:06:06,680 --> 00:06:08,480
Good boy, that's it!

98
00:06:09,580 --> 00:06:11,960
Still, you actually
built something like this

99
00:06:11,960 --> 00:06:15,860
If you'd put even a bit of
this passion into your work...

100
00:06:16,940 --> 00:06:18,920
I use it all the time, don't I?

101
00:06:21,920 --> 00:06:22,900
Sorry, sorry.

102
00:06:22,900 --> 00:06:24,840
Joe-chan!

103
00:06:28,600 --> 00:06:29,760
Ryo-san!

104
00:06:33,840 --> 00:06:35,120
What's going on?

105
00:06:36,300 --> 00:06:38,140
Are you alright, Ryo-san?

106
00:06:40,060 --> 00:06:41,440
I thought I was going to die.

107
00:06:42,380 --> 00:06:43,580
What about the helicopter?

108
00:06:44,660 --> 00:06:45,200
Helicopter?

109
00:06:45,620 --> 00:06:47,080
It flew right out the window!

110
00:06:47,820 --> 00:06:49,800
It cost a whopping 300,000 yen!

111
00:06:50,440 --> 00:06:52,340
If it's lost, you'll have to pay for it!

112
00:06:52,700 --> 00:06:54,160
You've got to be kidding!

113
00:06:54,860 --> 00:06:56,260
It's Ryo-chan's fault, isn't it?

114
00:06:56,480 --> 00:06:59,120
Damn it, where did it go?

115
00:07:00,740 --> 00:07:01,460
Oh!

116
00:07:02,040 --> 00:07:03,260
What a capable helicopter!

117
00:07:03,640 --> 00:07:05,040
It went and brought back friends!

118
00:07:11,960 --> 00:07:14,100
Damn you! How dare you take my helicopter!

119
00:07:14,460 --> 00:07:15,660
What's going on?

120
00:07:15,780 --> 00:07:18,180
W-what's this?
The helicopter's coming this way...

121
00:07:18,180 --> 00:07:19,040
What?

122
00:07:21,720 --> 00:07:22,680
What is that?

123
00:07:22,960 --> 00:07:24,560
Chief! Who on earth are they?

124
00:07:40,640 --> 00:07:41,860
It's the Black Hawk!

125
00:07:58,400 --> 00:08:00,650
Everyone,

126
00:08:00,700 --> 00:08:04,380
Sorry I'm late.

127
00:08:04,980 --> 00:08:08,272
starting today,
I'll be serving at this police box.

128
00:08:08,322 --> 00:08:09,340
I'm Keiichi Nakagawa.

129
00:08:10,640 --> 00:08:10,820
Nice to meet you.

130
00:08:10,820 --> 00:08:13,760
You there!
You went and destroyed my helicopter!

131
00:08:16,020 --> 00:08:18,540
Isn't that a Walther MPL submachine gun?

132
00:08:19,200 --> 00:08:21,600
You recognize it? That makes me happy!

133
00:08:22,080 --> 00:08:24,000
By the way, here's my handgun.

134
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:27,580
Isn't that the same one from Dirty Harry?

135
00:08:28,320 --> 00:08:30,260
That movie was amazing, wasn't it?

136
00:08:31,180 --> 00:08:34,220
If you like, I could give you one as an
apology for destroying your helicopter.

137
00:08:34,220 --> 00:08:36,640
Really? Well, thanks a lot!

138
00:08:36,640 --> 00:08:39,660
No, we have plenty more at home.

139
00:08:40,640 --> 00:08:41,200
Shall we go see it?

140
00:08:41,200 --> 00:08:42,460
Yes, let's go!

141
00:08:42,920 --> 00:08:45,460
Idiot!

142
00:08:46,420 --> 00:08:48,760
What the hell are you thinking?

143
00:08:48,760 --> 00:08:49,700
Recruitment

144
00:08:49,700 --> 00:08:50,980
Recruitment

145
00:08:50,980 --> 00:08:53,180
So this one's not allowed either?

146
00:08:55,080 --> 00:08:56,560
Of course not!

147
00:08:57,600 --> 00:08:58,220
Terai

148
00:08:58,220 --> 00:08:59,660
Go recruit.

149
00:09:00,260 --> 00:09:00,700
Yes.

150
00:09:03,220 --> 00:09:05,340
My stomach's cramping up again.

151
00:09:06,160 --> 00:09:07,500
I'm going to see a doctor, so

152
00:09:07,500 --> 00:09:09,640
Leave things to you.

153
00:09:10,840 --> 00:09:13,680
You've got some real potential, you know.

154
00:09:13,840 --> 00:09:15,940
I'm Ryotsu. Nice to meet you.

155
00:09:17,160 --> 00:09:19,820
So you're the famous Ryotsu-senpai?

156
00:09:20,860 --> 00:09:22,580
The pleasure's mine.

157
00:09:23,860 --> 00:09:25,920
Now we've got two little troublemakers.

158
00:09:26,620 --> 00:09:28,700
You don't seem too upset about it, though.

159
00:09:30,880 --> 00:09:34,080
Wow, that helicopter's privately owned?

160
00:09:36,020 --> 00:09:38,500
For a konjac shop, you're really well-off.

161
00:09:39,360 --> 00:09:40,260
Konjac shop?

162
00:09:41,840 --> 00:09:44,900
Anyway, Nakagawa,
why did you become a police officer?

163
00:09:46,240 --> 00:09:46,840
Well, you see,

164
00:09:48,040 --> 00:09:50,880
I lived in New York for many years,
where crime is rampant, so

165
00:09:50,880 --> 00:09:54,080
the policemen who risk their
lives fighting for the citizens

166
00:09:54,080 --> 00:09:56,120
have always been my idols.

167
00:10:00,040 --> 00:10:03,580
For a cop,
you sure wear a flashy uniform, don't you?

168
00:10:05,620 --> 00:10:08,760
Yeah, I'd say that's a bigger
problem than the handgun.

169
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:12,760
Really? Japanese police
uniforms are kind of lacking, so.

170
00:10:13,460 --> 00:10:15,220
I had it custom-made by Armani.

171
00:10:15,780 --> 00:10:16,700
Phew, phew, phew.

172
00:10:17,240 --> 00:10:18,740
I think it was about a million yen.

173
00:10:19,320 --> 00:10:22,300
Whoa! A million yen!?

174
00:10:22,300 --> 00:10:23,040
Haaah!

175
00:10:23,500 --> 00:10:26,980
I can't understand someone who spends that
much money on a uniform that's issued for free!

176
00:10:27,060 --> 00:10:30,400
I can't understand you either, Ryo-san,
spending 300,000 yen on a remote-control model.

177
00:10:30,820 --> 00:10:31,880
Don't lump me in with him!

178
00:10:32,120 --> 00:10:32,700
Yeah, yeah.

179
00:10:33,340 --> 00:10:34,640
Still, you know what

180
00:10:35,080 --> 00:10:39,080
I haven't been to the station lately, but you've
gotten pretty easygoing to allow clothes like that.

181
00:10:39,080 --> 00:10:41,785
Well, I was told in the
end it wasn't allowed, but -

182
00:10:41,835 --> 00:10:43,720
I changed clothes inside the helicopter.

183
00:10:44,060 --> 00:10:46,440
He went that far! Wahahaha!

184
00:10:46,940 --> 00:10:48,740
Well, hahahaha!

185
00:10:48,860 --> 00:10:50,880
The Chief's stomach must be hurting already.

186
00:10:53,460 --> 00:10:55,920
Yotchan,
make sure you teach Nakagawa properly.

187
00:10:56,860 --> 00:10:58,000
Have a good one.

188
00:10:59,580 --> 00:11:01,460
So what exactly should I be doing?

189
00:11:01,460 --> 00:11:03,120
Terai, I'll teach you.

190
00:11:03,120 --> 00:11:04,760
Ryo-san is supposed to
be the trainer, right?

191
00:11:05,100 --> 00:11:06,500
I'm off on patrol too.

192
00:11:06,960 --> 00:11:07,280
Hey.

193
00:11:09,180 --> 00:11:10,560
All of you, every last one.

194
00:11:11,640 --> 00:11:12,560
As for me...

195
00:11:14,060 --> 00:11:16,340
Stand out front and give
directions or something.

196
00:11:17,220 --> 00:11:17,540
Yes.

197
00:11:24,260 --> 00:11:27,180
Are you by any chance a police officer?

198
00:11:27,420 --> 00:11:28,420
Yes, I am.

199
00:11:28,880 --> 00:11:32,260
Thank goodness. I'd like to ask you for directions,
if I may.

200
00:11:33,220 --> 00:11:34,200
Yes, of course.

201
00:11:38,480 --> 00:11:40,820
Senpai, wake up, senpai!

202
00:11:42,120 --> 00:11:44,780
What is it? I was having such a nice sleep.

203
00:11:45,480 --> 00:11:47,270
An old man asked me for directions,

204
00:11:47,320 --> 00:11:50,080
but I'm totally clueless about this area.

205
00:11:51,800 --> 00:11:52,160
What?

206
00:11:52,760 --> 00:11:55,100
Show me the map and let me find it myself.

207
00:11:55,100 --> 00:11:58,740
He's an old man who just returned
to Japan after fifty years,

208
00:11:58,740 --> 00:12:01,140
and he says he doesn't
even know where he is.

209
00:12:02,300 --> 00:12:04,440
Geez, what a pain.

210
00:12:05,880 --> 00:12:07,120
So, where do you want to go?

211
00:12:07,700 --> 00:12:09,040
A restaurant, it is.

212
00:12:09,040 --> 00:12:10,660
What's the restaurant called?

213
00:12:10,660 --> 00:12:14,300
I've forgotten the name of the shop,
but the clue is,

214
00:12:17,260 --> 00:12:18,480
It's a shop like this.

215
00:12:20,080 --> 00:12:21,940
That's a really clumsy drawing, though.

216
00:12:21,940 --> 00:12:23,340
Did you draw it yourself?

217
00:12:23,580 --> 00:12:25,000
Back when I was a student.

218
00:12:25,000 --> 00:12:28,220
That was more than 50 years ago.

219
00:12:28,220 --> 00:12:30,240
What? 50 years?

220
00:12:31,400 --> 00:12:32,820
So, what's the shop's address?

221
00:12:33,080 --> 00:12:36,580
So it was in an old downtown area of Tokyo

222
00:12:36,580 --> 00:12:37,560
That's all you remember?

223
00:12:38,100 --> 00:12:38,500
Yes.

224
00:12:38,920 --> 00:12:39,840
No good, no good.

225
00:12:39,840 --> 00:12:41,640
Even the old downtown is big.

226
00:12:41,640 --> 00:12:43,060
There's no way anyone could know that.

227
00:12:43,500 --> 00:12:44,260
Give up.

228
00:12:44,260 --> 00:12:45,720
That won't do.

229
00:12:45,720 --> 00:12:48,320
After all, this is my very first job.

230
00:12:50,220 --> 00:12:52,320
If we were to look into it for you,

231
00:12:52,320 --> 00:12:55,580
I'd thought we'd show our appreciation,
wouldn't you say?

232
00:12:55,580 --> 00:12:57,980
Why didn't you say that first?

233
00:12:57,980 --> 00:13:00,560
Let's hear the details in the back.

234
00:13:01,140 --> 00:13:01,900
Hey, Nakagawa.

235
00:13:01,900 --> 00:13:04,260
Go order coffee and cake at the café.

236
00:13:04,700 --> 00:13:07,020
Just hurry up and go.

237
00:13:07,020 --> 00:13:07,560
Yes.

238
00:13:09,600 --> 00:13:10,000
I see.

239
00:13:12,040 --> 00:13:15,740
When I was a student at the art school,
I went to eat at that shop several times.

240
00:13:16,160 --> 00:13:16,900
Art school, you say?

241
00:13:16,900 --> 00:13:19,900
You mean what's now Tokyo
University of the Arts?

242
00:13:20,640 --> 00:13:23,520
Since it was during lunch break,
it was always crowded.

243
00:13:24,040 --> 00:13:26,560
So that means it was near the Geidai campus?

244
00:13:27,540 --> 00:13:31,220
If I recall,
it was about a fifteen-minute walk.

245
00:13:31,220 --> 00:13:33,720
Then it's the area up near Geidai.

246
00:13:37,760 --> 00:13:39,600
Here, why don't you take this too?

247
00:13:40,160 --> 00:13:40,940
Thanks, I appreciate it.

248
00:13:40,940 --> 00:13:44,600
Right, let's start searching
around Yanagawa Nezu.

249
00:13:45,450 --> 00:13:48,640
Do you think we'll find
it in about two hours?

250
00:13:49,040 --> 00:13:52,000
If it's Ueno, it's only 20 to 30 minutes by car,
so we'll be fine.

251
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:57,140
The truth is, I have to get back to
Paris on the 1 o'clock flight from Narita.

252
00:13:58,700 --> 00:14:03,560
From Ueno, it's just over an hour by limited express,
so we should manage.

253
00:14:03,560 --> 00:14:05,200
Hey, go catch a taxi!

254
00:14:05,200 --> 00:14:07,960
Then I'll call my car right away.

255
00:14:08,660 --> 00:14:11,860
Yes, it's me.
Bring the car to the police box right away.

256
00:14:13,860 --> 00:14:17,380
If you want, how about using mine?

257
00:14:17,380 --> 00:14:18,640
Thanks a lot!

258
00:14:21,380 --> 00:14:22,260
Arrived.

259
00:14:26,600 --> 00:14:29,300
It's a Ferrari F40!

260
00:14:29,920 --> 00:14:31,020
Please, young master, get in.

261
00:14:31,600 --> 00:14:33,080
But this is a two-seater, isn't it?

262
00:14:33,080 --> 00:14:36,140
It's been modified to seat four,
so it's fine.

263
00:14:36,640 --> 00:14:37,620
Come on, get in.

264
00:14:42,640 --> 00:14:44,380
Reiko, you're back at just the right time.

265
00:14:44,380 --> 00:14:45,400
Ryo-chan.

266
00:14:45,400 --> 00:14:47,260
I'm off to help someone. Mind the box.

267
00:14:48,460 --> 00:14:49,000
See you.

268
00:14:49,840 --> 00:14:50,200
Yeah.

269
00:14:51,960 --> 00:14:54,760
That man just now...
I feel like I've seen him somewhere.

270
00:14:59,880 --> 00:15:02,900
Damn it, I don't have time for this!

271
00:15:03,480 --> 00:15:05,440
Hey Nakagawa, turn there!

272
00:15:05,440 --> 00:15:07,120
Senpai, that's impossible!

273
00:15:07,120 --> 00:15:09,100
It's a one-way exit, though!

274
00:15:09,780 --> 00:15:10,720
You idiot!

275
00:15:11,860 --> 00:15:13,840
Don't you want to grant the old man's wish?!

276
00:15:14,020 --> 00:15:14,900
Well, no...

277
00:15:14,900 --> 00:15:16,900
Go in reverse! Then there's no problem!

278
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:18,060
B-but...

279
00:15:18,560 --> 00:15:21,360
Understood! Senpai!
We're going in reverse, then?!

280
00:15:27,480 --> 00:15:29,800
That bastard, how far is he going?

281
00:15:35,180 --> 00:15:36,020
Idiot, this is bad!

282
00:15:37,260 --> 00:15:39,460
I don't know...
I don't know anything about it...

283
00:15:46,020 --> 00:15:49,220
Wrong-way driving on a one-way street!

284
00:15:50,020 --> 00:15:53,520
Must be nice, riding around in
such an over-the-top bubble-era car.

285
00:15:53,520 --> 00:15:56,920
We don't have time to just watch!
This time we're making the arrest!

286
00:16:01,200 --> 00:16:03,380
Ferrari ahead, stop!

287
00:16:03,900 --> 00:16:05,420
Senpai, what should we do?

288
00:16:05,420 --> 00:16:10,440
Busy time for backing up! Come on! I'll
show you what the Ferrari can really do!

289
00:16:18,140 --> 00:16:19,180
Too fast!

290
00:16:19,800 --> 00:16:21,640
Ryotsu Kankichi again!

291
00:16:22,380 --> 00:16:24,980
Next time I see him,
I'm definitely arresting him!

292
00:16:27,140 --> 00:16:28,380
Okay, turn right at that corner.

293
00:16:28,380 --> 00:16:32,120
Left at the dead end up ahead.

294
00:16:32,980 --> 00:16:36,500
This maze of back alleys is so complicated,
yet you know it so well.

295
00:16:37,580 --> 00:16:40,140
I've been running around this
neighborhood since I was a kid.

296
00:16:43,080 --> 00:16:45,720
Even as a shortcut,
we can't go any further than this.

297
00:16:45,720 --> 00:16:48,300
You idiot, this is your first job!

298
00:16:48,840 --> 00:16:52,220
You know, once a police
officer takes on an assignment,

299
00:16:52,220 --> 00:16:55,240
no matter what happens,
they always see it through.

300
00:16:56,080 --> 00:16:59,200
Senpai, I was wrong.

301
00:17:00,500 --> 00:17:01,520
Alright!

302
00:17:05,820 --> 00:17:08,180
If it keeps getting narrower like this...

303
00:17:08,180 --> 00:17:11,140
Don't worry, we'll get through just fine.

304
00:17:12,220 --> 00:17:14,220
I've taken this route in
two or three moves before.

305
00:17:14,220 --> 00:17:15,180
On a bicycle.

306
00:17:15,180 --> 00:17:19,920
As expected of a senpai.

307
00:17:26,120 --> 00:17:29,260
Could you stop here for a sec?

308
00:17:31,080 --> 00:17:32,680
It brings back memories.

309
00:17:34,220 --> 00:17:36,600
I've lived in Paris for decades now,

310
00:17:36,600 --> 00:17:39,440
but lately I've been
thinking about Japan a lot.

311
00:17:40,600 --> 00:17:44,440
Back when I was an art school student,
full of dreams,

312
00:17:45,900 --> 00:17:49,840
I painted all day,
surrounded by good friends.

313
00:17:50,500 --> 00:17:53,120
Ueno really was a forest of art.

314
00:17:53,720 --> 00:17:56,280
I visited museums every day

315
00:17:56,280 --> 00:17:58,920
and debated art theory with my friends.

316
00:17:59,820 --> 00:18:03,460
Back then, there was a girl at
a cafeteria my friend took me to,

317
00:18:03,460 --> 00:18:05,620
and I fell for her at first sight.

318
00:18:06,320 --> 00:18:08,260
It was my first love, no doubt about it.

319
00:18:09,440 --> 00:18:14,440
So that's the cafeteria from the painting.
When was that again?

320
00:18:15,360 --> 00:18:21,140
I think it was close to graduation,
when I caught a cold and was bedridden.

321
00:18:22,080 --> 00:18:27,680
She came all the way to my
boarding house and nursed me.

322
00:18:32,580 --> 00:18:36,600
Once my cold got better,
I thought about thanking her,

323
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:41,000
but back then I was so poor I
couldn't afford a nice present.

324
00:18:41,860 --> 00:18:46,080
So I poured my feelings
into painting her portrait.

325
00:18:47,220 --> 00:18:49,160
And I gave her the painting.

326
00:18:50,600 --> 00:18:54,160
That girl's happy face from back then

327
00:18:54,680 --> 00:18:58,200
is still burned clearly into my eyelids,
even now.

328
00:18:59,060 --> 00:19:00,860
So what happened with that girl?

329
00:19:01,680 --> 00:19:05,340
Right after graduating,
I went off to study in Paris.

330
00:19:05,800 --> 00:19:07,840
I never even told her I liked her.

331
00:19:09,240 --> 00:19:11,420
It's a story from long, long ago.

332
00:19:11,420 --> 00:19:14,400
Old man,
this is no time to be lost in admiring art!

333
00:19:14,400 --> 00:19:16,360
We've got barely an hour left!

334
00:19:18,220 --> 00:19:19,560
Let's look for a cafeteria.

335
00:19:20,380 --> 00:19:20,820
Yeah.

336
00:19:24,200 --> 00:19:25,440
Well, old man?

337
00:19:25,880 --> 00:19:27,720
Does any of this scenery
look familiar to you?

338
00:19:30,920 --> 00:19:33,920
This area has changed a lot
since fifty years ago, so...

339
00:19:36,980 --> 00:19:38,180
One hour left

340
00:19:48,720 --> 00:19:49,920
It's hopeless, isn't it.

341
00:19:50,820 --> 00:19:54,820
I suppose I'll just keep these memories
as memories and take them back to Paris.

342
00:19:55,700 --> 00:19:58,280
There's still ten minutes! I won't give up!

343
00:19:58,980 --> 00:20:00,260
I'm not giving up!

344
00:20:00,760 --> 00:20:02,920
I can find one or two ways!

345
00:20:03,140 --> 00:20:04,840
A police officer!

346
00:20:05,160 --> 00:20:06,420
As if he could handle the job!

347
00:20:07,180 --> 00:20:09,020
Damn it!

348
00:20:12,820 --> 00:20:15,680
My first love,
whom I've held in my heart for fifty years,

349
00:20:16,720 --> 00:20:18,280
I really wish I could
have introduced you to her.

350
00:20:18,280 --> 00:20:19,740
It's all right.

351
00:20:19,740 --> 00:20:22,060
It's just fate, I suppose.

352
00:20:23,640 --> 00:20:24,480
That tree.

353
00:20:24,480 --> 00:20:32,120
Look, this shop.

354
00:20:32,840 --> 00:20:34,420
It's exactly like the painting!

355
00:20:35,420 --> 00:20:35,840
Yeah.

356
00:20:35,840 --> 00:20:37,400
It hasn't changed one bit.

357
00:20:38,720 --> 00:20:39,280
Well then.

358
00:20:39,730 --> 00:20:41,180
Let's go see your first love.

359
00:20:41,180 --> 00:20:43,340
Wait a moment.

360
00:20:43,340 --> 00:20:45,180
What's wrong, old man?

361
00:20:45,180 --> 00:20:47,080
Well, she's probably already...

362
00:20:48,280 --> 00:20:52,020
She probably has plans too,
and showing up out of the blue like this...

363
00:20:52,520 --> 00:20:54,740
After all this trouble,
what are you talking about!

364
00:20:55,100 --> 00:20:56,040
Come on, inside.

365
00:20:56,040 --> 00:20:57,460
But...

366
00:20:57,460 --> 00:20:59,640
If you won't open it,
old man, I'll open it myself.

367
00:21:00,580 --> 00:21:01,080
Come on.

368
00:21:05,880 --> 00:21:09,180
Open it, hurry up and open it, you dimwit!

369
00:21:15,360 --> 00:21:16,140
Miss...

370
00:21:16,800 --> 00:21:19,900
Mr. Taki... It's you, Mr. Taki, isn't it?

371
00:21:21,020 --> 00:21:21,620
Yes.

372
00:21:22,240 --> 00:21:24,100
It's been a long time.

373
00:21:24,100 --> 00:21:26,040
Yes, it really has.

374
00:21:26,040 --> 00:21:27,395
Mr. Taki, that painting...

375
00:21:27,445 --> 00:21:30,080
We still have it hanging in the shop.

376
00:21:35,040 --> 00:21:38,880
You've been taking good care of it.

377
00:21:39,560 --> 00:21:42,420
That painting is my treasure.

378
00:21:42,420 --> 00:21:43,320
Thank you.

379
00:21:45,580 --> 00:21:46,940
Thank you, Ms. Mizutani.

380
00:21:50,520 --> 00:21:52,140
Senpai, look at this.

381
00:21:52,140 --> 00:21:54,200
at that happy face.

382
00:21:55,840 --> 00:22:00,140
That's what we police officers work so hard for,
the smiles of the citizens.

383
00:22:00,140 --> 00:22:03,380
Being a police officer is a wonderful job,
isn't it?

384
00:22:03,880 --> 00:22:07,260
By the way, old man, how much are
you going to give us as a thank-you?

385
00:22:08,560 --> 00:22:09,660
S-senpai!

386
00:22:10,540 --> 00:22:13,820
No, thanks to you,
I've made a wonderful memory.

387
00:22:14,300 --> 00:22:16,840
Please accept this as
a token of my gratitude.

388
00:22:16,840 --> 00:22:19,460
No, thank you, thank you.

389
00:22:19,460 --> 00:22:21,440
Well then, I'll be going now.

390
00:22:21,440 --> 00:22:23,620
Thank you for all your help.

391
00:22:24,280 --> 00:22:25,480
Take care.

392
00:22:25,480 --> 00:22:26,700
Goodbye.

393
00:22:28,720 --> 00:22:30,080
Come on, let's head back.

394
00:22:32,600 --> 00:22:33,860
I'll come visit again.

395
00:22:35,300 --> 00:22:37,980
Hey, I'm not happy about this one bit.

396
00:22:39,660 --> 00:22:40,800
Apparently he got something

397
00:22:43,100 --> 00:22:43,980
Oi, young fella.

398
00:22:45,040 --> 00:22:46,140
I'm giving you this painting.

399
00:22:46,820 --> 00:22:48,720
Are you sure? It's such a precious one.

400
00:22:48,720 --> 00:22:50,640
It's fine. Go on, take it.

401
00:22:54,820 --> 00:22:56,700
Jotaro Taki

402
00:22:58,340 --> 00:23:00,880
So the Ferrari just got
totally dented in the end

403
00:23:01,480 --> 00:23:02,740
It's no big deal.

404
00:23:02,740 --> 00:23:05,560
We still have more cars than
we know what to do with at home.

405
00:23:05,560 --> 00:23:07,520
Is your family really that rich?

406
00:23:08,380 --> 00:23:08,760
Yeah, I suppose.

407
00:23:09,660 --> 00:23:12,440
Our assets come to roughly 400 trillion yen,
I think.

408
00:23:12,440 --> 00:23:13,980
400 trillion yen?

409
00:23:14,480 --> 00:23:16,880
Nakagawa, let's be friends.

410
00:23:16,880 --> 00:23:19,320
Ryo-chan, this is serious! Serious!

411
00:23:19,320 --> 00:23:21,620
You know that old man we
gave the Ferrari ride to?

412
00:23:22,180 --> 00:23:23,720
That shabby old geezer?

413
00:23:23,720 --> 00:23:27,980
He was an incredibly famous painter known around the world,
you know!

414
00:23:28,860 --> 00:23:30,500
Yeah, that's definitely him.

415
00:23:31,560 --> 00:23:33,360
Is he really that famous of a painter?

416
00:23:33,740 --> 00:23:37,500
Apparently one of his paintings
is worth at least 100 million yen.

417
00:23:37,500 --> 00:23:39,300
W-100 million yen!

418
00:23:40,220 --> 00:23:41,640
Ugh, here it comes!

419
00:23:42,120 --> 00:23:44,740
Ugh, h-hey, Ryotsu!

420
00:23:45,260 --> 00:23:47,680
The adrenaline's really going to kick in,
so hang on!

421
00:23:48,120 --> 00:23:50,080
My 100 million yen!

422
00:23:50,480 --> 00:24:07,000
I've just come up with something amazing!

423
00:24:07,500 --> 00:24:09,440
We'll ride a hot air balloon and sell ramen.

424
00:24:09,440 --> 00:24:11,320
In other words, a flying convenience store.

425
00:24:11,320 --> 00:24:14,540
How about that? Nobody else could
have thought of an idea this brilliant!

426
00:24:14,960 --> 00:24:17,220
Ryotsu Kankichi, the great genius!

427
00:24:17,220 --> 00:24:21,460
Look forward to our next episode,
the flying food stall that'll be a huge hit!

428
00:24:32,920 --> 00:24:36,700
Always keep on smiling, okay?

429
00:24:37,500 --> 00:24:40,900
Even when something outrageous happens,

430
00:24:40,900 --> 00:24:45,420
keep smiling sweetly, okay?

431
00:24:45,420 --> 00:24:50,640
just head out with a
look like nothing's wrong.

432
00:24:50,640 --> 00:24:54,160
Hey, smile for me.

433
00:24:54,160 --> 00:24:57,540
It's not your fault.

434
00:24:59,080 --> 00:25:02,840
Hey, smile for me.

435
00:25:02,840 --> 00:25:05,800
Just like you were a moment ago.

436
00:25:07,500 --> 00:25:16,600
Keep smiling all the time, because a
woman who acts so serious isn't beautiful.

437
00:25:16,600 --> 00:25:25,840
You should smile right away,
unless you're still a child.

438
00:25:37,540 --> 00:25:41,280
Thank you for watching.

